Assistant (8) 2026-11-04 16:29:24.414 UTC (+750.2s)

I resolved the conflicts and committed the result as one new commit, caddaf09c29, on top of the conflict commit in      
/workspace. I could only check it by compiling parts of it. The ML-DSA tests were not run, because there is no built JDK
or jtreg here.                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
/repo is mounted read-only and sits on a different branch, so I did the work in /workspace, which has                   
backport-a269fa0-java17 checked out. No conflict markers remain in src, test, closed or make.                           
                                                                                                                        
- X509Authentication.java: the conflict was only the copyright line. I kept the 2026 year and the new MLDSA entry from  
  the original change.                                                                                                  
- DefaultSSLConfigSignatureSchemes.java: I deleted it. The original change only edited this file, but on this branch it 
  was never added. It comes from 8366364, which this release doesn't have, and it depends on                            
  SSLConfiguration#getSSLParameters() returning signature schemes, which this branch's version doesn't do. Leaving it   
  would add a test that fails.                                                                                          
- SignatureScheme.java, getParams() calls: the file had no conflict, but the original code wouldn't compile on Java 17. 
  It calls getParams() directly on PrivateKey and PublicKey, which only exists from Java 22. I switched both calls to   
  KeyUtil.getParams(Key), which already exists on this branch and finds the method by reflection.                       
- SignatureScheme.java, logging: the original also used the newer SSLLogger.isOn() and SSLLogger.Opt.HANDSHAKE_VERBOSE  
  API. This branch uses the SSLLogger.isOn field and string checkpoints, so I used SSLLogger.isOn &&                    
  SSLLogger.isOn("ssl,handshake,verbose").                                                                              
- Other dependencies: the ML-DSA provider classes, NamedParameterSpec and NamedPKCS8Key/NamedX509Key are all present.   
  The SSLContextTemplate.java changes and the five new MLDSA* tests are identical to the originals and use nothing newer
  than Java 17.                                                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
For the compile check I built SignatureScheme.java, X509Authentication.java and KeyUtil.java against the Java 17        
runtime. javac reported no errors in those three files. It did report errors in unrelated JDK sources that need         
generated files, which I ignored.                                                                                       
